Fix CDP mouse event screen coordinates: use real screen space

CDP-dispatched mouse events carried the widget-relative position as the
screen position (screenX == clientX). A page can compare
event.screenX - event.clientX against window.screenX / window.screenY and
flag the mismatch as soon as the browser window sits anywhere but the
screen origin - a trivially scriptable automation fingerprint. Real OS
input always satisfies screenX == clientX + window content origin, so
convert via the view bounds exactly like the touch dispatch path already
does (ConvertWidgetPointToScreenPoint). Applied in
InputHandler::HandleMouseEvent so both InputHandler::DispatchMouseEvent
and the InputInjector drag flow are covered; the method already
guarantees widget_host->GetView() is non-null.

diff --git a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/input_handler.cc b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/input_handler.cc
index 9364acb..972bc82 100644
--- a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/input_handler.cc
+++ b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/input_handler.cc
@@ -1402,6 +1402,14 @@ void InputHandler::HandleMouseEvent(
     return;
   }
 
+  // Use real screen coordinates: CDP-dispatched mouse events previously carried the
+  // widget position as the screen position (screenX == clientX), which contradicts
+  // the page-visible window.screenX / window.screenY once the browser window sits
+  // anywhere but the screen origin, a detectable automation fingerprint. Mirrors the
+  // touch dispatch path, which already converts via ConvertWidgetPointToScreenPoint.
+  event->SetPositionInScreen(ConvertWidgetPointToScreenPoint(
+      CHECK_DEREF(widget_host->GetView()), event->PositionInWidget()));
+
   auto findWidgetAndDispatchEvent = base::BindOnce(
       [](base::WeakPtr<InputHandler> self,
          base::WeakPtr<RenderWidgetHostImpl> widget_host,
